.el .ds Aq '
.TH shiftpaper-set 1  shiftpaper 
.SH NAME
shiftpaper\-set \- Bake an image and set it as the active wallpaper
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshiftpaper set\fR [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bake an image and set it as the active wallpaper.
.PP
Performs the same baking as `bake`, then points the daemon\*(Aqs config.toml at it, replacing any slideshow, and a running daemon changes to it. The resolved model path is also persisted to [inference] so future invocations don\*(Aqt need \-\-model.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
Path to the ONNX depth model. Falls back to $SHIFTPAPER_MODEL, then [inference] model_path in config.toml. When provided, the resolved path is persisted to config
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
Source image (jpeg, png, or webp)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
shiftpaper set ~/Pictures/forest.jpg
shiftpaper set forest.jpg \-\-model ~/models/other.onnx
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
shiftpaper(1)
.PP
The docs: https://github.com/CPritch/shiftpaper/tree/main/docs
